<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk.Web">

    <PropertyGroup>
        <TargetFramework>net9.0</TargetFramework>
        <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
        <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
        <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>

        <!--
        AOT smoke test #4 (GH-4778).

        Wolverine.AotSmoke.Publish covers the MESSAGING entry path in a real
        native image. This one covers the HTTP entry path, which was the gap that
        let GH-4752 and GH-4778 both reach us from a user's production publish:
        every existing AOT smoke references Wolverine.csproj alone, so
        HttpGraph.DiscoverEndpoints (the frame at the top of both reported stack
        traces) never executed in a native image in CI.

        What it pins: an HTTP endpoint whose return type implements
        IResponseAware makes HttpChain close Applier of that type while the chain
        MODEL is built, which happens at startup even under TypeLoadMode.Static
        with the generated code already compiled in. Nothing names that
        instantiation statically, so without the rooting block
        HttpEndpointRegistryCodeFile now emits, ILC trims it and
        MapWolverineEndpoints throws. The reported case is an endpoint returning
        Marten's UpdatedAggregate; a local IResponseAware reaches the identical
        code with no store in the picture, which is what keeps this project cheap
        enough to gate on.

        Deliberately boots and serves one real request rather than only
        constructing the host: the crash is in MapWolverineEndpoints, but a
        request proves the response-aware rewrite produced a working endpoint
        rather than merely a discoverable one.

        Refresh the committed pre-gen FROM THIS PROJECT'S DIRECTORY, because a
        host writes relative to the working directory, not the project folder:

          dotnet run -f net9.0 codegen write

        then commit the result. This project carries NO hand-written roots, so a
        regression in the emitted rooting block fails the lane outright instead
        of hiding behind a hand-written one.
        -->
        <PublishAot>true</PublishAot>
        <StripSymbols>false</StripSymbols>
        <InvariantGlobalization>true</InvariantGlobalization>

        <!-- Runtime behaviour of a native image is what this asserts. The trim-analysis warning wall is
             Wolverine.AotSmoke's job; here it would only bury the signal. Mirrors
             Wolverine.AotSmoke.Publish. -->
        <SuppressTrimAnalysisWarnings>true</SuppressTrimAnalysisWarnings>

        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);IL2026;IL2046;IL2055;IL2065;IL2067;IL2070;IL2072;IL2075;IL2087;IL2090;IL2091;IL2104;IL2111;IL3000;IL3050;IL3051;IL3053</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>

    <ItemGroup>
        <ProjectReference Include="..\..\Http\Wolverine.Http\Wolverine.Http.csproj" />
    </ItemGroup>

</Project>
